unlike|different-from|PREPOSITION|Different from|Different from the person or thing that follows.|không giống; khác với|Unlike the old tent, this one has room to stand upright.|Không giống chiếc lều cũ, chiếc này có chỗ để đứng thẳng.|Unlike plus noun phrase; unlike her brother. Do not confuse with dislike, which is usually a verb.|0
wizard|magical-person|NOUN|Magical person|A person in stories who is believed to have magical powers.|phù thủy; người có phép thuật|The wizard in the play changed a broken cup into a bird.|Phù thủy trong vở kịch biến một chiếc cốc vỡ thành một con chim.|Countable; a wizard. Commonly male in traditional stories, but usage varies in fictional worlds.|-
wizard|highly-skilled-person|NOUN|Highly skilled person|A person who is exceptionally good at a particular activity.|người rất giỏi; bậc thầy|Our neighbour is a wizard at repairing old radios.|Hàng xóm của chúng tôi rất giỏi sửa radio cũ.|Informal, often approving; a wizard at something, a computer wizard.|-
instant|immediate|ADJECTIVE|Immediate|Happening or available with almost no delay.|ngay lập tức; tức thì|The new ticket machine gave an instant confirmation.|Máy bán vé mới đưa ra xác nhận ngay lập tức.|Usually before a noun; instant response, instant access. Instantly is the adverb.|0
instant|quickly-prepared-food|ADJECTIVE|Quickly prepared food|Prepared so that it can be made ready quickly, often by adding liquid.|ăn liền; hòa tan|She packed instant soup for the overnight trip.|Cô ấy mang súp ăn liền cho chuyến đi qua đêm.|Instant coffee, instant noodles; generally before a food or drink noun.|1
instant|very-short-time|NOUN|Very short time|A very short period or a particular moment.|khoảnh khắc; chốc lát|For an instant, the room fell completely silent.|Trong một khoảnh khắc, căn phòng hoàn toàn im lặng.|Countable; an instant, in an instant, at that instant. Distinct from the adjective describing immediacy.|-
pound|british-currency-unit|NOUN|British currency unit|The basic monetary unit of the United Kingdom.|bảng Anh|The used book cost three pounds at the market.|Cuốn sách cũ có giá ba bảng Anh ở chợ.|Countable; one pound, three pounds. The symbol £ precedes the amount.|0
pound|weight-unit|NOUN|Unit of weight|A unit of weight in customary systems equal to sixteen ounces in common everyday use.|pao; đơn vị khối lượng pound|The package weighed just over a pound on the old scale.|Bưu kiện nặng hơn một pao một chút trên chiếc cân cũ.|Countable; two pounds, abbreviated lb. Distinguish this weight unit from the currency unit.|1
pound|strike-repeatedly|VERB|Strike repeatedly|To hit something again and again with force.|đập mạnh liên tục; giã|He pounded the wooden peg into the soft ground.|Anh ấy đập liên tục để đóng chiếc cọc gỗ vào đất mềm.|Transitive pound something or intransitive pound on a door. Pounded and pounding are regular forms.|-
stall|small-selling-stand|NOUN|Small selling stand|A small stand or partly enclosed space where goods are sold.|quầy hàng; sạp hàng|The fruit stall stood beside the entrance to the market.|Sạp trái cây nằm bên lối vào chợ.|Countable; a market stall, a stall selling flowers.|0
stall|engine-stops-running|VERB|Engine stops running|For an engine to stop operating unexpectedly, or to make it do so.|chết máy; làm chết máy|The old van stalled while the driver was reversing.|Chiếc xe tải nhỏ cũ chết máy khi người lái đang lùi xe.|Intransitive the engine stalled or transitive stall the engine. The cause is not specified by the verb alone.|-
stall|delay-progress|VERB|Delay progress|To deliberately delay action or prevent something from progressing.|trì hoãn; câu giờ|The speaker stalled by asking for another copy of the agenda.|Người phát biểu câu giờ bằng cách xin thêm một bản chương trình nghị sự.|Intransitive stall for time; transitive stall negotiations. Distinct from an engine stopping.|-
